<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="[scrollbar-gutter:stable]">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <.live_title suffix=" · Phoenix Framework">
      {assigns[:page_title] || "Livedj"}
    </.live_title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/app.css"} />
    <script
      defer
      phx-track-static
      type="text/javascript"
      src={~p"/assets/app.js"}
    >
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="antialiased overflow-hidden bg-tone-100 dark:bg-tone-900">
    {@inner_content}
    <div
      id="video-player-hook"
      phx-hook="Youtube"
      phx-update="ignore"
      class="mx-1 w-[98%] h-72 relative flex my-2"
    >
      <div class="w-full">
        <div
          id="player-container"
          class="w-full h-72 rounded-lg transition duration-1000 hidden mr-1"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        id="player-backdrop"
        phx-hook="PlayerBackdrop"
        class="absolute w-full h-full bg-black rounded-lg overflow-hidden"
      >
        <canvas
          id="player-spinner"
          class="hidden absolute inset-0 w-full h-full rounded-lg"
        />
      </div>
      <%!--
        Sibling of #player-backdrop (not nested inside it) so it never
        inherits the backdrop's own opacity-0/opacity-50 toggling from
        play/pause state - it needs to stay fully legible on its own.

        The positioning (absolute inset-0) lives on this plain, non-focusable
        wrapper rather than on the button itself: .focus-ignite forces
        `position: relative` on its host (it's unlayered CSS, so it beats
        Tailwind's layered `.absolute` utility outright), which would fight
        the button for its own positioning and collapse it into normal flex
        flow, shrinking the video box next to it.

        Initial visibility is decided here from @media_loaded? (computed at
        mount from the real player state), not left to default-visible +
        JS: this div is phx-update="ignore", so whatever renders first is
        what sticks until youtube/hook.js's load_video handler catches up -
        defaulting to visible would flash the hint over an already-loaded
        room on every page load.
      --%>
      <div
        id="player-hint-container"
        class={[
          "absolute inset-0 z-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 pointer-events-none rounded-lg",
          !assigns[:media_loaded?] && "bg-black"
        ]}
      >
        <button
          id="player-empty-hint"
          type="button"
          class={[
            "flex flex-col items-center gap-2",
            "text-tone-100/80 hover:text-tone-100 cursor-pointer pointer-events-auto",
            "rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-ignite",
            assigns[:media_loaded?] && "hidden"
          ]}
        >
          <.icon name="hero-plus-circle" class="h-8 w-8" />
          <span
            id="player-empty-hint-text"
            class="text-sm font-medium"
            data-first-video-text={gettext("Click + to add your first video")}
            data-another-video-text={gettext("Click + to add a video")}
          >
            <%= if assigns[:playlist_has_media?] do %>
              {gettext("Click + to add a video")}
            <% else %>
              {gettext("Click + to add your first video")}
            <% end %>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <%!-- Out-of-sync notification banner --%>
      <div
        id="out-of-sync-banner"
        class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 mx-2 hidden z-20"
      >
        <div class="
          flex items-center justify-between gap-2
          bg-red-300/90 text-red-100
          rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm shadow-lg
        ">
          <span id="out-of-sync-message"></span>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0">
            <button
              id="resync-btn"
              class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-white cursor-pointer"
            >
              {gettext("Resync")}
            </button>
            <button
              id="out-of-sync-dismiss"
              class="text-lg leading-none opacity-70 hover:opacity-100 cursor-pointer"
              aria-label="Dismiss"
            >
              ×
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
